@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+## #1951 - A batch suite step starts its test executable from the build's cargo JSON artifacts
+
+**What was decided.**
+
+- Each batch prebuild (`debug build: <crate> (--no-run)`) has the flag
+  `--message-format=json-render-diagnostics`. The executor keeps the JSON messages of the build and makes
+  one `cargo metadata --no-deps` call. From the two it records the test executables of the crate
+  (`xtask/src/artifacts.rs`).
+- A suite step of that crate (`--lib`, `--bins` or `--test <name>`) then starts the recorded executable
+  and does not start cargo (`xtask/src/direct.rs`). The step name, the step number, the log file name and
+  the plan are the same. `--dry-run` prints the same cargo commands.
+- The executable starts as `cargo test` starts it: in the package directory, with the libtest args after
+  `--`, and with the variables that cargo sets (`CARGO`, `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, `CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH`, the
+  `CARGO_PKG_*` set, `CARGO_BIN_EXE_<bin>`, `OUT_DIR`, the `rustc-env` pairs of the build script and the
+  dynamic library path). The list was read from a test process under cargo 1.100.
+- The gate writes cargo's `Running <target> (<path>)` line into the step log before the output of the
+  executable. `read_log`, the notes and `--failed` read the log as before.
+- A step stays a cargo step when one of these is true: its package has no recorded build in this run
+  (`--only` or `--failed` selected the step without its build step); its target has no executable in the
+  list; it is a `--doc` step; its args are not exactly the known form. The printed command shows which
+  way a step ran.
+- The executable path comes only from the JSON list. The gate never searches `target/` for one.
+- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` makes each step a cargo step again. It is for a comparison run, and for a
+  platform where a direct run does not behave as `cargo test` does. This PR ran on macOS only.
+
+**Why.**
+
+- Each suite step started cargo to run one binary that was built already. The issue gives about 0.5 s for
+  one start on Windows, and the batch plan has several hundred suite steps.
+- This PR is stacked on #2788. That PR builds each crate alone, so the executables of the build are the
+  same ones that `cargo test -p <crate>` runs. With one build for all the crates the features are
+  unified, and the executables are different ones.
+- cargo 1.100 puts a test executable in `target/debug/build/<pkg>/<hash>/out/`, not in
+  `target/debug/deps/`. A path that the gate computes itself is wrong on one of the two layouts. The JSON
+  list is correct on the two.
+- When the gate runs under `cargo xtask`, its own process has the `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` and `CARGO_PKG_*`
+  values of `xtask`. A direct run must set the values of the tested package. If not, a test that reads
+  one of them at run time gets the wrong value.
+
+**Considered and dropped.**
+
+- The release tier. Its debug build is one build for all the crates (feature unification). Its steps
+  stay cargo steps. A change to builds for each crate changes the plan of the cut gate; that is not in
+  this issue.
+- The heavy lanes (`--release --ignored`) and the quick tier. They have other build steps and few steps
+  for each run. `direct::records` and `direct::of` accept a step only by its args, so a later PR can add
+  the JSON flag to those builds.
+- A new dependency (`serde_json`, `cargo_metadata`). The gate reads a few fields. `xtask/src/json.rs` is
+  a small reader for them.
+- A search for `*-<hash>` files in `target/`. It can find an old executable or the GUI binary.
+- A hard failure when a target has no recorded executable. cargo runs the step correctly in that case,
+  and the printed command shows it.
+- A `rustc --print target-libdir` call for the library path. Under `cargo xtask` the path of the gate
+  process has the toolchain directories already. The tests link no toolchain dylib.
+
+**Cost to change later.**
+
+- Low. Remove the JSON flag from `plan::debug_build_crate`, and each step is a cargo step again.
+- The `gate` skill text still says that each step calls `cargo test`. The worker session could not edit
+  `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md` (the edit was refused). The text needs an update.
+- If a later cargo sets a new variable for a test process, add it in `artifacts::package`.
diff --git a/xtask/src/artifacts.rs b/xtask/src/artifacts.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..5503cc650
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xtask/src/artifacts.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,162 @@
+//! The test executables of one crate, read from the JSON messages of its `cargo test --no-run` build,
+//! and the variables that cargo gives a test process of that crate (#1951). A test executable is only
+//! ever taken from this list: the gate never searches `target/` for one (a glob can start the GUI).
+//! Provenance: the Cargo Book ("JSON messages", "cargo metadata", "Environment variables Cargo sets for
+//! crates"); the run-time variables were read from a test process under cargo 1.100.
+
+use std::collections::HashMap;
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+
+use crate::json::{self, Json};
+
+/// One test executable and the text of cargo's `Running` line for it (`unittests src/lib.rs`,
+/// `tests/smoke.rs`), which the gate writes into the step log so the notes read as before.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct TestExe {
+    pub exe: PathBuf,
+    pub label: String,
+}
+
+/// What one build recorded for one package.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct Package {
+    /// The manifest directory: cargo starts each test process of the package there.
+    pub dir: PathBuf,
+    pub lib: Vec<TestExe>,
+    pub bins: Vec<TestExe>,
+    /// The integration binaries by target name (`--test <name>`).
+    pub tests: Vec<(String, TestExe)>,
+    /// The variables cargo sets for a test process, the `CARGO` path excluded.
+    pub env: Vec<(String, String)>,
+    /// The directories cargo puts first on the dynamic library path.
+    pub lib_paths: Vec<PathBuf>,
+}
+
+impl Package {
+    pub fn count(&self) -> usize {
+        self.lib.len() + self.bins.len() + self.tests.len()
+    }
+}
+
+/// The recorded builds of one gate run, by package name (`camcraft-app`).
+pub type Built = HashMap<String, Package>;
+
+const LIB_KINDS: &[&str] = &["lib", "rlib", "dylib", "cdylib", "staticlib", "proc-macro"];
+
+fn kinds(target: &Json) -> Vec<&str> {
+    target.get("kind").map(Json::items).unwrap_or(&[]).iter().filter_map(Json::str).collect()
+}
+
+/// `1.2.3-rc.1+build` as the `CARGO_PKG_VERSION_*` parts (major, minor, patch, pre).
+fn version_parts(version: &str) -> [String; 4] {
+    let core = version.split('+').next().unwrap_or("");
+    let (nums, pre) = core.split_once('-').unwrap_or((core, ""));
+    let mut n = nums.split('.');
+    let mut part = || n.next().unwrap_or("").to_string();
+    [part(), part(), part(), pre.to_string()]
+}
+
+/// The package `name` from the text of `cargo metadata --no-deps` and the JSON `messages` of its build.
+/// `Err` names what is missing; the caller then leaves the steps of the package with cargo.
+pub fn package(name: &str, metadata: &str, messages: &str) -> Result<Package, String> {
+    let meta = json::parse(metadata.trim()).ok_or("cargo metadata did not print JSON")?;
+    let pkg = meta
+        .get("packages")
+        .map(Json::items)
+        .unwrap_or(&[])
+        .iter()
+        .find(|p| p.text("name") == Some(name))
+        .ok_or_else(|| format!("cargo metadata has no package {name}"))?;
+    let manifest = pkg.text("manifest_path").ok_or("cargo metadata gives no manifest_path")?;
+    let id = pkg.text("id").unwrap_or("");
+    let dir = Path::new(manifest).parent().ok_or("the manifest has no directory")?.to_path_buf();
+    let version = pkg.text("version").unwrap_or("");
+    let [major, minor, patch, pre] = version_parts(version);
+    let authors: Vec<&str> = pkg.get("authors").map(Json::items).unwrap_or(&[]).iter().filter_map(Json::str).collect();
+    let field = |k: &str| pkg.text(k).unwrap_or("").to_string();
+    let mut env: Vec<(String, String)> = vec![
+        ("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR".into(), dir.to_string_lossy().into_owned()),
+        ("CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH".into(), manifest.to_string()),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_NAME".into(), name.to_string()),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION".into(), version.to_string()),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_MAJOR".into(), major),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_MINOR".into(), minor),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_PATCH".into(), patch),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_PRE".into(), pre),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_AUTHORS".into(), authors.join(":")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_DESCRIPTION".into(), field("description")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_HOMEPAGE".into(), field("homepage")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_REPOSITORY".into(), field("repository")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_LICENSE".into(), field("license")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_LICENSE_FILE".into(), field("license_file")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_RUST_VERSION".into(), field("rust_version")),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_README".into(), field("readme")),
+    ];
+    let target_dir = meta.text("target_directory").map(PathBuf::from);
+    let mut out = Package { dir: dir.clone(), ..Package::default() };
+    let mut finished = false;
+    for line in messages.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with('{')) {
+        let Some(m) = json::parse(line) else { continue };
+        match m.text("reason") {
+            Some("compiler-artifact") if m.text("manifest_path") == Some(manifest) => {
+                let (Some(target), Some(exe)) = (m.get("target"), m.text("executable")) else { continue };
+                let (kind, tname) = (kinds(target), target.text("name").unwrap_or(""));
+                if !m.get("profile").and_then(|p| p.get("test")).is_some_and(Json::is_true) {
+                    // The plain binary of the package: cargo names it to the test process.
+                    if kind.contains(&"bin") {
+                        env.push((format!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_{tname}"), exe.to_string()));
+                    }
+                    continue;
+                }
+                let src = Path::new(target.text("src_path").unwrap_or(""));
+                let rel = src.strip_prefix(&dir).unwrap_or(src).to_string_lossy().replace('\\', "/");
+                let unit = TestExe { exe: PathBuf::from(exe), label: format!("unittests {rel}") };
+                if kind.contains(&"test") {
+                    out.tests.push((tname.to_string(), TestExe { label: rel, ..unit }));
+                } else if kind.contains(&"bin") {
+                    out.bins.push(unit);
+                } else if kind.iter().any(|k| LIB_KINDS.contains(k)) {
+                    out.lib.push(unit);
+                }
+            }
+            Some("build-script-executed") => {
+                for p in m.get("linked_paths").map(Json::items).unwrap_or(&[]).iter().filter_map(Json::str) {
+                    // `native=/path`, `dependency=/path`, ... or a bare path; cargo keeps those in the target dir.
+                    let path = PathBuf::from(p.split_once('=').map_or(p, |(_, v)| v));
+                    if target_dir.as_ref().is_some_and(|t| path.starts_with(t)) && !out.lib_paths.contains(&path) {
+                        out.lib_paths.push(path);
+                    }
+                }
+                if m.text("package_id") == Some(id) {
+                    if let Some(dir) = m.text("out_dir") {
+                        env.push(("OUT_DIR".into(), dir.to_string()));
+                    }
+                    for pair in m.get("env").map(Json::items).unwrap_or(&[]) {
+                        if let [k, v] = pair.items()
+                            && let (Some(k), Some(v)) = (k.str(), v.str())
+                        {
+                            env.push((k.to_string(), v.to_string()));
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+            Some("build-finished") => {
+                if !m.get("success").is_some_and(Json::is_true) {
+                    return Err("the build did not finish with success".into());
+                }
+                finished = true;
+            }
+            _ => {}
+        }
+    }
+    if !finished {
+        return Err("the build printed no build-finished message".into());
+    }
+    if let Some(t) = target_dir {
+        // The profile directory (and `deps` in the older layout), where cargo puts the workspace's dylibs.
+        out.lib_paths.push(t.join("debug"));
+        out.lib_paths.push(t.join("debug").join("deps"));
+    }
+    out.env = env;
+    Ok(out)
+}
diff --git a/xtask/src/artifacts_tests.rs b/xtask/src/artifacts_tests.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..090be38e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xtask/src/artifacts_tests.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,215 @@
+//! Provenance: issue #1951 - reading cargo's JSON artifact list and choosing the steps that run a test
+//! executable directly. The message texts are in the form that cargo 1.100 prints (Windows paths included).
+
+use std::ffi::OsString;
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+
+use crate::artifacts::{self, Built, Package, TestExe};
+use crate::direct;
+use crate::json::{self, Json};
+use crate::plan::{self, Step};
+
+#[test]
+fn json_reads_cargo_lines_and_refuses_bad_text() {
+    let v = json::parse(r#" {"a":"C:\\x\\y.exe","b":[true,null,-1.5e1],"c":{"d":"q\"\u00e9\ud83d\ude00\n"}} "#).expect("valid");
+    assert_eq!(v.text("a"), Some(r"C:\x\y.exe"));
+    assert_eq!(v.get("b").map(Json::items), Some(&[Json::Bool(true), Json::Null, Json::Num(-15.0)][..]));
+    assert_eq!(v.get("c").and_then(|c| c.text("d")), Some("q\"\u{e9}\u{1F600}\n"));
+    assert_eq!(v.text("b"), None, "an array is not a string");
+    assert_eq!(json::parse("[]"), Some(Json::Arr(Vec::new())));
+    for bad in ["", "{", "{\"a\":}", "[1,]", "\"open", "{\"a\":1} x", "\"\\q\"", "nul", "\"\\u12\"", "--", "{\"a\" 1}"] {
+        assert_eq!(json::parse(bad), None, "{bad:?} is not JSON");
+    }
+    let deep = format!("{}{}", "[".repeat(5000), "]".repeat(5000));
+    assert_eq!(json::parse(&deep), None, "deep nesting is refused, not a stack overflow");
+}
+
+const META: &str = r#"{"packages":[
+ {"name":"camcraft-cl","version":"0.1.0","id":"path+file:///w/crates/cl#camcraft-cl@0.1.0","manifest_path":"/w/crates/cl/Cargo.toml","authors":[]},
+ {"name":"camcraft-app","version":"0.24.1-rc.2+b7","id":"path+file:///w/crates/app#camcraft-app@0.24.1-rc.2","license":"MIT","license_file":null,
+  "description":"the app","manifest_path":"/w/crates/app/Cargo.toml","authors":["A","B"],"readme":"README.md","repository":null,"homepage":null,"rust_version":"1.90"}],
+ "target_directory":"/w/target","workspace_root":"/w"}"#;
+
+fn artifact(manifest: &str, kind: &str, name: &str, src: &str, test: bool, exe: Option<&str>) -> String {
+    let exe = exe.map_or("null".to_string(), |e| format!("\"{e}\""));
+    format!(
+        r#"{{"reason":"compiler-artifact","package_id":"x","manifest_path":"{manifest}","target":{{"kind":["{kind}"],"name":"{name}","src_path":"{src}"}},"profile":{{"test":{test}}},"filenames":[],"executable":{exe},"fresh":true}}"#
+    )
+}
+
+fn messages(finished: &str) -> String {
+    let app = "/w/crates/app/Cargo.toml";
+    [
+        "   Compiling camcraft-app v0.24.1 (not JSON: skipped)".to_string(),
+        artifact("/w/crates/cl/Cargo.toml", "lib", "camcraft_cl", "/w/crates/cl/src/lib.rs", true, Some("/w/target/debug/deps/camcraft_cl-1")),
+        artifact(app, "custom-build", "build-script-build", "/w/crates/app/build.rs", false, None),
+        r#"{"reason":"build-script-executed","package_id":"other","linked_paths":["native=/w/target/debug/build/flecs/out","/elsewhere/lib"],"env":[["NOT_OURS","1"]],"out_dir":"/w/target/o"}"#.to_string(),
+        r#"{"reason":"build-script-executed","package_id":"path+file:///w/crates/app#camcraft-app@0.24.1-rc.2","linked_paths":[],"env":[["APP_BUILT","yes"]],"out_dir":"/w/target/debug/build/app/out"}"#.to_string(),
+        artifact(app, "lib", "camcraft_app", "/w/crates/app/src/lib.rs", false, None),
+        artifact(app, "bin", "camcraft-cli", "/w/crates/app/src/bin/cli.rs", false, Some("/w/target/debug/camcraft-cli")),
+        artifact(app, "lib", "camcraft_app", "/w/crates/app/src/lib.rs", true, Some("/w/target/debug/deps/camcraft_app-2")),
+        artifact(app, "bin", "camcraft-cli", "/w/crates/app/src/bin/cli.rs", true, Some("/w/target/debug/deps/camcraft_cli-3")),
+        artifact(app, "test", "smoke", "/w/crates/app/tests/smoke.rs", true, Some("/w/target/debug/deps/smoke-4")),
+        artifact(app, "example", "demo", "/w/crates/app/examples/demo.rs", true, Some("/w/target/debug/examples/demo-5")),
+        finished.to_string(),
+    ]
+    .join("\n")
+}
+
+const OK: &str = r#"{"reason":"build-finished","success":true}"#;
+
+fn app() -> Package {
+    artifacts::package("camcraft-app", META, &messages(OK)).expect("recorded")
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn package_takes_only_its_own_test_executables_from_the_json() {
+    let p = app();
+    assert_eq!(p.dir, PathBuf::from("/w/crates/app"));
+    let exe = |p: &TestExe| p.exe.to_string_lossy().into_owned();
+    assert_eq!(p.lib.iter().map(exe).collect::<Vec<_>>(), ["/w/target/debug/deps/camcraft_app-2"]);
+    assert_eq!(p.bins.iter().map(exe).collect::<Vec<_>>(), ["/w/target/debug/deps/camcraft_cli-3"], "the test build of the bin, not the app itself");
+    assert_eq!(p.tests.len(), 1);
+    assert_eq!((p.tests[0].0.as_str(), exe(&p.tests[0].1)), ("smoke", "/w/target/debug/deps/smoke-4".to_string()));
+    assert_eq!(p.count(), 3, "no example, no build script, no other package, no plain binary");
+    // The labels are cargo's `Running` texts.
+    assert_eq!(p.lib[0].label, "unittests src/lib.rs");
+    assert_eq!(p.bins[0].label, "unittests src/bin/cli.rs");
+    assert_eq!(p.tests[0].1.label, "tests/smoke.rs");
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn package_gives_the_variables_of_a_cargo_test_process() {
+    let p = app();
+    let var = |k: &str| p.env.iter().find(|(n, _)| n == k).map(|(_, v)| v.as_str());
+    for (k, want) in [
+        ("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR", "/w/crates/app"),
+        ("CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH", "/w/crates/app/Cargo.toml"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_NAME", "camcraft-app"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION", "0.24.1-rc.2+b7"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_MAJOR", "0"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_MINOR", "24"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_PATCH", "1"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_VERSION_PRE", "rc.2"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_AUTHORS", "A:B"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_DESCRIPTION", "the app"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_HOMEPAGE", ""),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_REPOSITORY", ""),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_LICENSE", "MIT"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_LICENSE_FILE", ""),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_RUST_VERSION", "1.90"),
+        ("CARGO_PKG_README", "README.md"),
+        ("CARGO_BIN_EXE_camcraft-cli", "/w/target/debug/camcraft-cli"),
+        ("OUT_DIR", "/w/target/debug/build/app/out"),
+        ("APP_BUILT", "yes"),
+    ] {
+        assert_eq!(var(k), Some(want), "{k}");
+    }
+    assert_eq!(var("NOT_OURS"), None, "the build script variables of another package stay out");
+    let want = ["/w/target/debug/build/flecs/out", "/w/target/debug", "/w/target/debug/deps"];
+    assert_eq!(p.lib_paths, want.map(PathBuf::from), "linked paths in the target dir (not /elsewhere), then the profile dirs");
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn package_refuses_a_build_that_did_not_finish_or_a_package_it_does_not_know() {
+    let red = artifacts::package("camcraft-app", META, &messages(r#"{"reason":"build-finished","success":false}"#));
+    assert_eq!(red, Err("the build did not finish with success".into()));
+    assert_eq!(artifacts::package("camcraft-app", META, &messages("")), Err("the build printed no build-finished message".into()));
+    assert_eq!(artifacts::package("camcraft-ui", META, &messages(OK)), Err("cargo metadata has no package camcraft-ui".into()));
+    assert_eq!(artifacts::package("camcraft-app", "not json", &messages(OK)), Err("cargo metadata did not print JSON".into()));
+}
+
+fn built() -> Built {
+    Built::from([("camcraft-app".to_string(), app())])
+}
+
+fn suite(sel: &[&str]) -> Step {
+    let mut args = vec!["test", "-j", "2", "-p", "camcraft-app", "--no-fail-fast"];
+    args.extend(sel);
+    args.extend(["--", "--test-threads=2"]);
+    Step::new("app suites: x", &args, "app")
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn only_a_single_crate_debug_build_with_json_records() {
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&plan::debug_build_crate("app")), Some("camcraft-app".into()));
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&plan::debug_build(&["cl", "app"])), None, "the release tier's one build does not ask for JSON");
+    let two = Step::new("b", &["test", "-p", "camcraft-cl", "-p", "camcraft-app", "--no-run", direct::JSON], "");
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&two), None, "a build of several crates unifies features: its executables are other ones");
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&Step::new("b", &["test", "--no-run", direct::JSON], "")), None, "no package named");
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&Step::new("b", &["test", "-p", "camcraft-app", "--no-run"], "")), None, "no JSON, no record");
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&Step::new("b", &["test", "--release", "-p", "camcraft-app", "--no-run", direct::JSON], "")), None);
+    assert_eq!(direct::records(&suite(&["--lib"])), None);
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn a_debug_target_step_of_a_recorded_package_runs_its_executable() {
+    let b = built();
+    let of = |s: &Step| direct::of(s, &s.args, &b, "the-cargo");
+    let d = of(&suite(&["--test", "smoke"])).expect("direct");
+    assert_eq!(d.exes, [b["camcraft-app"].tests[0].1.clone()]);
+    assert_eq!(d.cwd, b["camcraft-app"].dir, "cargo starts a test in the package directory");
+    assert_eq!(d.args, ["--test-threads=2"], "the libtest args after `--` are kept");
+    assert_eq!(d.env[0], ("CARGO".to_string(), OsString::from("the-cargo")));
+    assert!(d.env.iter().any(|(k, v)| k == "CARGO_PKG_NAME" && v == "camcraft-app"));
+    assert!(d.env.iter().any(|(k, _)| k == direct::LIB_PATH_VAR));
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--lib"])).map(|d| d.exes), Some(b["camcraft-app"].lib.clone()));
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--bins"])).map(|d| d.exes), Some(b["camcraft-app"].bins.clone()));
+    // Cargo keeps every step that is not exactly one recorded debug target.
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--doc"])), None, "doctests have no executable");
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--test", "not_built"])), None, "no executable in the list: never a guess at a path");
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--test", "smoke", "--release"])), None);
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--test", "smoke", "--features", "x"])), None, "an arg the gate does not know stays with cargo");
+    assert_eq!(of(&suite(&["--lib", "--test", "smoke"])), None, "two targets are one cargo step");
+    assert_eq!(of(&Step::new("s", &["test", "-j", "2", "-p", "camcraft-app", "--test", "smoke", "--", "--test-threads=2"], "")), None, "fail-fast stays with cargo");
+    assert_eq!(of(&Step::new("s", &["test", "-j", "2", "-p", "camcraft-cl", "--no-fail-fast", "--lib"], "")), None, "no build of this package was recorded");
+    assert_eq!(of(&Step::new("c", &["clippy", "-p", "camcraft-app"], "")), None);
+    let mut known = suite(&["--test", "smoke"]);
+    known.expect_fail = Some(crate::known_fail::KnownFail { issue: 1, dir: "app".into(), target: "smoke".into(), test: "t".into(), file: "f".into(), line: 1, reason: "r".into() });
+    assert_eq!(of(&known), None, "a known-fail check stays as it is");
+    assert_eq!(direct::of(&suite(&["--lib"]), &suite(&["--lib"]).args, &Built::new(), "c"), None);
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn the_batch_plan_records_each_crate_and_keeps_its_steps() {
+    let root = Path::new(env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")).parent().expect("workspace");
+    let p = plan::batch(root);
+    let builds: Vec<&Step> = p.steps.iter().filter(|s| crate::lanes::is_build(s)).collect();
+    assert!(!builds.is_empty() && builds.iter().all(|s| direct::records(s).is_some()), "each batch prebuild records its artifacts");
+    // With every target in the list, each suite step but a `--doc` one is a direct run; nothing else is.
+    let mut all = Built::new();
+    for s in &p.steps {
+        let Some(key) = crate::lanes::target_key(s) else { continue };
+        let (dir, target) = key.split_once(':').expect("dir:target");
+        let pkg = all.entry(plan::pkg(dir)).or_default();
+        let exe = TestExe { exe: PathBuf::from(format!("/t/{dir}-{target}")), label: target.to_string() };
+        match target {
+            "lib" => pkg.lib.push(exe),
+            "bins" => pkg.bins.push(exe),
+            "doc" => {}
+            _ => pkg.tests.push((target.to_string(), exe)),
+        }
+    }
+    let mut direct_steps = 0;
+    for s in &p.steps {
+        let d = direct::of(s, &s.args, &all, "cargo");
+        let suite = s.name.contains(" suites: ") && !s.name.ends_with(": doc");
+        assert_eq!(d.is_some(), suite, "{}", s.name);
+        direct_steps += usize::from(d.is_some());
+    }
+    assert!(direct_steps > 100, "the batch suites are several hundred steps: {direct_steps}");
+    let release = plan::release(root);
+    assert!(release.steps.iter().all(|s| direct::records(s).is_none()), "the release tier is not changed: its one debug build unifies features");
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn lib_path_puts_the_build_dirs_first_and_keeps_the_current_value() {
+    let first = [PathBuf::from("/t/debug"), PathBuf::from("/t/debug/deps")];
+    let cur = std::env::join_paths(["/tool/lib", "/usr/lib"]).expect("join");
+    let got = direct::lib_path(&first, Some(cur), None).expect("joined");
+    let dirs: Vec<PathBuf> = std::env::split_paths(&got).collect();
+    assert_eq!(dirs, ["/t/debug", "/t/debug/deps", "/tool/lib", "/usr/lib"].map(PathBuf::from));
+    let unset: Vec<PathBuf> = std::env::split_paths(&direct::lib_path(&first, None, Some("/home/u".into())).expect("joined")).collect();
+    assert_eq!(&unset[..2], &first[..]);
+    assert_eq!(unset.len() > 2, cfg!(target_os = "macos"), "only macOS gets cargo's default fallback dirs");
+}
diff --git a/xtask/src/direct.rs b/xtask/src/direct.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4c0853960
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xtask/src/direct.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,190 @@
+//! Starting the process of a gate step: cargo, or - for one debug test target of a crate whose build
+//! step recorded its artifacts - the test executable itself, as `cargo test` starts it: in the package
+//! directory, with cargo's variables, its args after `--` (#1951). One cargo start costs about 0.5 s
+//! on Windows, and batch has several hundred such steps.
+//! Provenance: our own build law (AGENTS.md "Three gate tiers"); the Cargo Book (`cargo test`, "JSON
+//! messages", "Environment variables"); libtest's CLI.
+
+use std::ffi::OsString;
+use std::fs::File;
+use std::io::Write;
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+use std::process::{Command, Stdio};
+
+use crate::artifacts::{self, Built, Package, TestExe};
+use crate::plan::Step;
+
+/// The cargo flag of a build step whose test executables the gate records.
+pub const JSON: &str = "--message-format=json-render-diagnostics";
+
+/// The package of a build step that records: a debug `--no-run` build of exactly one package with
+/// `JSON`. A build of several packages unifies their features, so its executables are not the ones
+/// that `cargo test -p <one crate>` runs (#2727); it never records.
+pub fn records(s: &Step) -> Option<String> {
+    let a = &s.args;
+    let flag = |f: &str| a.iter().any(|x| x == f);
+    if !(flag("--no-run") && flag(JSON)) || flag("--release") {
+        return None;
+    }
+    let mut pkgs = a.windows(2).filter(|w| w[0] == "-p").map(|w| w[1].clone());
+    let one = pkgs.next()?;
+    pkgs.next().is_none().then_some(one)
+}
+
+/// `CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT=1` makes each step a cargo step again (a comparison run, or a platform where
+/// a direct run does not behave as `cargo test`).
+pub const OPT_OUT: &str = "CAMCRAFT_GATE_NO_DIRECT";
+
+pub fn opted_out() -> bool {
+    std::env::var_os(OPT_OUT).is_some_and(|v| v == "1")
+}
+
+/// `of`, unless the environment opts out.
+pub fn chosen(s: &Step, args: &[String], built: &Built, cargo: &str) -> Option<Direct> {
+    if opted_out() { None } else { of(s, args, built, cargo) }
+}
+
+/// A step as a direct run: the executables (in cargo's order), their working directory, args and variables.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub struct Direct {
+    pub exes: Vec<TestExe>,
+    pub cwd: PathBuf,
+    pub args: Vec<String>,
+    pub env: Vec<(String, OsString)>,
+}
+
+/// The direct run of `s` (`args` are its scaled args), or `None` when cargo must run it: a step that is
+/// not exactly `test -j N -p <pkg> --no-fail-fast (--lib | --bins | --test <name>) [-- <libtest args>]`
+/// (so `--release`, `--doc`, a quick or known-fail step), a package without a recorded build in this run
+/// (`--only` / `--failed` left its build step out), or a target without an executable in the list.
+pub fn of(s: &Step, args: &[String], built: &Built, cargo: &str) -> Option<Direct> {
+    if s.expect_fail.is_some() {
+        return None;
+    }
+    let split = args.iter().position(|a| a == "--").unwrap_or(args.len());
+    let mut it = args[..split].iter().map(String::as_str);
+    if it.next() != Some("test") {
+        return None;
+    }
+    let (mut pkg, mut target, mut keep_going) = (None, None, false);
+    while let Some(a) = it.next() {
+        match a {
+            "-j" => drop(it.next()?),
+            "-p" if pkg.is_none() => pkg = Some(it.next()?),
+            "--no-fail-fast" => keep_going = true,
+            "--lib" | "--bins" if target.is_none() => target = Some((a, "")),
+            "--test" if target.is_none() => target = Some((a, it.next()?)),
+            _ => return None,
+        }
+    }
+    let p: &Package = built.get(pkg?)?;
+    let exes: Vec<TestExe> = match target? {
+        ("--lib", _) => p.lib.clone(),
+        ("--bins", _) => p.bins.clone(),
+        (_, name) => p.tests.iter().filter(|(n, _)| n == name).map(|(_, e)| e.clone()).collect(),
+    };
+    if exes.is_empty() || !keep_going {
+        return None;
+    }
+    let mut env: Vec<(String, OsString)> = vec![("CARGO".into(), cargo.into())];
+    env.extend(p.env.iter().map(|(k, v)| (k.clone(), OsString::from(v))));
+    if let Some(v) = lib_path(&p.lib_paths, std::env::var_os(LIB_PATH_VAR), std::env::var_os("HOME")) {
+        env.push((LIB_PATH_VAR.into(), v));
+    }
+    Some(Direct { exes, cwd: p.dir.clone(), args: args.get(split + 1..).unwrap_or(&[]).to_vec(), env })
+}
+
+/// The variable of the dynamic library search path, as cargo chooses it.
+pub const LIB_PATH_VAR: &str = if cfg!(windows) {
+    "PATH"
+} else if cfg!(target_os = "macos") {
+    "DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH"
+} else {
+    "LD_LIBRARY_PATH"
+};
+
+/// `first` before the current value of the variable. Under `cargo xtask` that value already has the
+/// toolchain's library directories. On macOS an unset variable gets the system's default fallback, as
+/// cargo adds it. `None` when a path cannot be joined: the variable then stays as it is.
+pub fn lib_path(first: &[PathBuf], current: Option<OsString>, home: Option<OsString>) -> Option<OsString> {
+    let mut all: Vec<PathBuf> = first.to_vec();
+    match current {
+        Some(v) => all.extend(std::env::split_paths(&v)),
+        None if cfg!(target_os = "macos") => {
+            all.extend(home.map(|h| PathBuf::from(h).join("lib")));
+            all.extend([PathBuf::from("/usr/local/lib"), PathBuf::from("/usr/lib")]);
+        }
+        None => {}
+    }
+    std::env::join_paths(all).ok()
+}
+
+/// The line the gate prints for a direct step.
+pub fn describe(d: &Direct, root: &Path) -> String {
+    let exes: Vec<String> = d.exes.iter().map(|e| shown(&e.exe, root)).collect();
+    format!("{} {} (direct, from the build's cargo JSON artifacts)", exes.join(" + "), d.args.join(" "))
+}
+
+fn shown(p: &Path, root: &Path) -> String {
+    p.strip_prefix(root).unwrap_or(p).to_string_lossy().replace('\\', "/")
+}
+
+/// Runs each executable of `d` with its output in `log`, after a `Running` line in cargo's form. All of
+/// them run (the step has `--no-fail-fast`). The exit code of the first one that failed, else 0. An
+/// executable that cannot start is an `error:` line in the log and code -1: a red step, never a pass.
+pub fn run(d: &Direct, root: &Path, mut log: File) -> Result<i32, String> {
+    let io = |e: std::io::Error| format!("gate log: {e}");
+    let mut code = 0;
+    for t in &d.exes {
+        writeln!(log, "     Running {} ({})", t.label, shown(&t.exe, root)).map_err(io)?;
+        let status = Command::new(&t.exe)
+            .args(&d.args)
+            .envs(d.env.iter().map(|(k, v)| (k, v)))
+            .current_dir(&d.cwd)
+            .stdin(Stdio::null())
+            .stdout(log.try_clone().map_err(io)?)
+            .stderr(log.try_clone().map_err(io)?)
+            .status();
+        let one = match status {
+            Ok(st) => st.code().unwrap_or(-1),
+            Err(e) => {
+                writeln!(log, "error: could not start the test executable {}: {e}", t.exe.display()).map_err(io)?;
+                -1
+            }
+        };
+        if code == 0 {
+            code = one;
+        }
+    }
+    Ok(code)
+}
+
+/// Runs `cargo <args>` in `dir` with its output in `log`. With `capture`, stdout (the JSON messages of
+/// a recording build) comes back as text and only stderr (the build's readable output) goes to the log.
+pub fn cargo(cargo: &str, env: Vec<(&'static str, String)>, args: &[String], dir: &Path, log: File, capture: bool) -> Result<(i32, Option<String>), String> {
+    let fail = |e: std::io::Error| format!("cargo {}: {e}", args.join(" "));
+    let mut cmd = Command::new(cargo);
+    cmd.envs(env).args(args).current_dir(dir).stdin(Stdio::null());
+    if capture {
+        let out = cmd.stdout(Stdio::piped()).stderr(log).output().map_err(fail)?;
+        return Ok((out.status.code().unwrap_or(-1), Some(String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).into_owned())));
+    }
+    let err = log.try_clone().map_err(fail)?;
+    let status = cmd.stdout(log).stderr(err).status().map_err(fail)?;
+    Ok((status.code().unwrap_or(-1), None))
+}
+
+/// The package of a green recording build, from its JSON `messages` and one `cargo metadata --no-deps`
+/// call in `root` (the package fields of cargo's variables). `Err` says why nothing was recorded.
+pub fn record(root: &Path, cargo: &str, name: &str, messages: &str) -> Result<Package, String> {
+    let out = Command::new(cargo)
+        .args(["metadata", "--no-deps", "--format-version", "1"])
+        .current_dir(root)
+        .stdin(Stdio::null())
+        .output()
+        .map_err(|e| format!("cargo metadata: {e}"))?;
+    if !out.status.success() {
+        return Err(format!("cargo metadata failed: {}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr).trim()));
+    }
+    artifacts::package(name, &String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout), messages)
+}
